# Sub-agent routing (mandatory)

Before implementing a domain change, **delegate or follow the owning agent**. Do not cross module DB boundaries.

| Area / path | Sub-agent |
| --- | --- |
| Requirements, workflows, phasing, PRD | `product-architect` |
| Design system, tokens, screen UX | `ui-design-agent` |
| `apps/web/(pos)`, `(scan)`, cart/offline/shortcuts | `frontend-pos-agent` |
| Products, variants, brands, prices | `catalog-agent` |
| Stock ledger, transfers, counts, serial status | `inventory-agent` |
| Barcode/QR/labels/scan helpers | `barcode-agent` |
| Sales, checkout, refunds, shifts, payments records | `sales-agent` |
| Suppliers, POs, receiving | `purchasing-agent` |
| Customers, loyalty, warranty profile | `customer-agent` |
| Guliosmart sync, VFD/EFD, MM APIs, worker sync | `integration-agent` |
| Auth, roles, audit, abuse | `security-agent` |
| Tests / E2E | `qa-agent` |
| Docker, nginx, backup, monitoring | `devops-agent` |

## Delegation examples

- “Add IMEI on receive” → `purchasing-agent` + `inventory-agent`
- “POS cart shortcuts” → `frontend-pos-agent` (+ `ui-design-agent` if visual)
- “Website stock sync” → `integration-agent`
- “product.stock -= 1” → **reject**; route to `inventory-agent`

Agents live in `.cursor/agents/`. Full memory: root `AGENTS.md`.
